  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This grant supports Armed Conflict Location and Event Data Project (ACLED) to strengthen access to timely, high quality data on conflict and political violence worldwide.  ACLED is a leading provider of real-time, open-access data and analysis, supporting evidence-based policymaking, early warning, and conflict prevention efforts.  Irelands&#x2019; funding supports ACLED&apos;s core analytical capacity, including coverage of conflict-affected and under reported contexts and the production of rigorous and, accessible analysis.  This partnership reflects Ireland&apos;s commitment to peace promotion, civilian protection, and the use of robust evidence to inform international engagement and diplomacy.</narrative>
  </description>
